      "text": "Loki wagered his head with the dwarf Brok that Brok's brother Sindre would not be able to make three treasures as good as the hair, Skidbladner, and Gungner.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "In the smithy, Sindre laid a pig-skin in the furnace and ordered Brok to blow the bellows without stopping until he returned.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "While Brok worked the bellows, a fly landed on his hand and stung him, but he continued blowing until Sindre removed from the furnace a boar with golden bristles.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Next Sindre put gold in the furnace, again instructing Brok to keep the bellows going; a fly stung Brok on the neck, but he persisted, and Sindre produced the ring Draupner.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "Finally Sindre put iron into the furnace, warning that all would be worthless if the bellows stopped; a fly stung Brok between the eyes so that blood ran into them, causing him briefly to let go, and Sindre then took a hammer from the furnace that had come near being spoiled.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "Sindre gave the boar, ring, and hammer to Brok and sent him with Loki to Asgard to settle the wager.",
