      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:7",
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "When Loki and Brok presented the treasures in Asgard, the gods sat upon their doom-steads and agreed that Odin, Thor, and Frey would decide the outcome.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "Loki gave the spear Gungner to Odin, Sif's golden hair to Thor, and Skidbladner to Frey, explaining that Gungner never misses, the hair will grow once placed on Sif's head, and Skidbladner always has a fair wind and can be folded up and carried in a pocket.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:9"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "Brok gave Odin the ring Draupner, which drops eight other rings of equal weight every ninth night; he gave Frey the boar, which can run through air and over sea, night or day, faster than any horse and whose golden bristles provide light even in the worlds of darkness; and he gave Thor the hammer, which can strike any target without being damaged, always returns to the thrower, and can shrink to be concealed, though it has a short handle.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "The gods decided that the hammer was the best of all the treasures and the greatest protection against the frost-giants, and they declared that the dwarf had fairly won the wager.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "Loki offered to ransom his head, but Brok refused; Loki then tried to escape using shoes that let him run through the air and over the sea, yet Thor seized him at the dwarf's request.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "When Brok wanted to cut off Loki's head, Loki argued that his head, but not his neck, had been pledged in the wager.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "Brok attempted to pierce Loki's lips with a knife in order to sew his mouth shut, but the knife would not cut; after he mentioned needing his brother's awl, it appeared, allowing him to pierce the lips, and he sewed Loki's mouth together with a thread that he broke off at the end; this thread is called Vartare ('a strap').",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": [
        "ev:12"
