    "summary": "Ivan Tsarevich departs from his bird-form brothers-in-law, leaving a silver fork and a gold ring as tokens indicating his fate, and travels to reclaim his wife Marya Morevna from Koshchéi Without-Death. Despite multiple attempts to flee with Marya while Koshchéi is away hunting, a prophetic horse warns the antagonist, who repeatedly overtakes them and finally kills Ivan, dismembers him, seals him in a tarred, iron-hooped barrel, and casts it into the blue sea. The tokens darken at his brothers-in-law's homes, prompting the Eagle, Falcon, and Raven to retrieve the barrel, reassemble Ivan's body, and resurrect him using dead water to knit the flesh and living water to restore life. Ivan immediately resumes his quest, asking Marya to discover how Koshchéi obtained his extraordinary steed. Marya cleverly learns from Koshchéi of Baba-Yaga, who lives beyond the thrice-ninth land and thirtieth kingdom, past a fiery river, and possesses world-circling mares. She also learns of Koshchéi's magic kerchief that creates a fire-proof bridge over the river. Marya secretly takes the kerchief and gives it to Ivan, who uses it to cross the fiery river on a magical bridge and go to Baba-Yaga. On his long, foodless journey, Ivan spares a chick belonging to a bird from beyond the sea, after she promises future service, and then approaches a swarm of bees intending to take honey.",
    "language": "English",
    "quote_policy": "summarized"
  },
  "literal_observations": [
    {
      "id": "obs:1",
      "text": "Ivan Tsarevich stays three days with his bird-form relatives and then announces that he is going to seek his wife, Marya Morevna.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:2",
      "text": "The Eagle asks Ivan to leave his silver fork so they can look at it and remember him.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:3",
      "text": "Ivan leaves the silver fork with the Eagle and travels for several days.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:4",
      "text": "After traveling, Ivan sees a castle with an oak beside it, on which a raven is perched; the raven flies down, strikes the earth, and transforms into a gallant youth.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:5",
      "text": "The youth who was a raven calls to Anna Tsarevna, saying their brother is coming.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:6",
      "text": "Anna Tsarevna joyfully meets Ivan, kisses and embraces him, asks about his health, and tells him about her life and household.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:3"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:7",
      "text": "Ivan stays three days with Anna Tsarevna and the Raven, then says farewell and declares he is going to look for his wife, Marya Morevna.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:4"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:8",
      "text": "The Raven asks Ivan to leave his gold ring with them, saying they will look at it and remember him, and that its brightness will show he is alive and well while dimness will signal evil.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:4"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:9",
      "text": "Ivan leaves his gold ring with the Raven and travels for three days until he reaches Marya Morevna.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:4", "ev:5"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Seeing Ivan, Marya Morevna rushes to him, cries, and reproaches him for disobeying her by looking in the closet and releasing Koshchéi Without-Death.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:5"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Ivan asks Marya to forgive him, urges her not to remember the past, and proposes that they flee while Koshchéi is absent, hoping he will not overtake them.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:5"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:12",
      "text": "As Koshchéi returns from hunting, his good steed stumbles, and Koshchéi asks if the horse feels misfortune.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:6"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:13",
      "text": "The horse tells Koshchéi that Ivan Tsarevich has taken Marya Morevna and says Koshchéi could sow wheat, wait for it to ripen, reap and thresh it, make flour, bake five ovens of bread, eat the bread, then pursue and still overtake them.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:6"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:14",
      "text": "Koshchéi gallops, overtakes Ivan and Marya, forgives Ivan the first time for giving him water and a second time, but warns that on the third he will hew him to pieces, then takes Marya back.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:7"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:15",
      "text": "Ivan repeatedly returns to take Marya away when Koshchéi is not at home; Marya warns that Koshchéi will overtake them and hew Ivan to pieces, but Ivan insists he cannot live without her.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:8", "ev:9"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:16",
      "text": "Each time Koshchéi rides home, his horse stumbles and reports that Ivan has taken Marya away, adding that barley could be sown, harvested, brewed into beer, drunk, and sleep taken before pursuing and still catching them.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:8"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:17",
      "text": "On the third pursuit, Koshchéi overtakes Ivan, hews him into small pieces, places them in a pitched barrel strengthened with iron hoops, and casts the barrel into the blue sea, taking Marya home.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:9"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "At the houses of Ivan's brothers-in-law, the silver grows black, and they conclude that some evil has happened.",
      "category": "attribute",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:10"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "The Eagle rushes to the blue sea, retrieves the barrel, and brings it to shore; the Falcon fetches living water, and the Raven fetches dead water.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:11"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "The three brothers-in-law break the barrel, wash Ivan's pieces, and put them together; the Raven sprinkles the body with dead water so it grows together, and the Falcon sprinkles it with living water so Ivan trembles, rises, and speaks.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:11"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:21",
      "text": "Ivan remarks that he has slept a long time, and the brothers-in-law reply that he would have slept longer without them, then invite him to their houses; Ivan declines, saying he will go to seek Marya Morevna.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:11", "ev:12"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:22",
      "text": "Ivan tells Marya to discover from Koshchéi Without-Death where he found his steed.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:13"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:23",
      "text": "Marya uses a favorable moment to ask Koshchéi, who explains that beyond the thrice-ninth land, in the thirtieth kingdom, beyond a fiery river, lives Baba-Yaga, who has a mare that flies around the world daily and many other glorious mares; he served her as herdsman for three days, kept the mares from straying, and received a colt as a reward.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:14"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:24",
      "text": "Marya asks Koshchéi how he crossed the fiery river, and he says he has a kerchief that, when waved three times on the right side, makes a lofty bridge that the fire cannot reach.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:15"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:25",
      "text": "Marya tells Ivan everything she has learned, secretly takes the kerchief, gives it to Ivan, and Ivan uses it to cross the fiery river and go to Baba-Yaga.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:16"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:26",
      "text": "On his long journey without eating or drinking, Ivan meets a bird from beyond the sea with her little children, intends to eat one chick, but refrains when the bird begs him not to and promises to serve him in time.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:17"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:27",
      "text": "Ivan continues and sees a swarm of bees in the forest, saying he will take some honey.",
      "category": "action",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:18"]
    }
  ],
