    {
      "id": "obs:10",
      "text": "Hogni describes the place of Sigurd's body where eagles (ernes) scream, ravens croak, and wolves howl over Gudrun's husband.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:8"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:11",
      "text": "Gudrun reproaches Hogni for telling her of such misery and curses his heart, wishing ravens to tear it and that he should have no men to travel with him.",
