    {
      "id": "obs:18",
      "text": "Grimhild, Queen of Gothland, hears of Gudrun's sorrowful abiding, pushes the cloth away, calls her sons, and eagerly asks who will atone for her son and her slain lord by paying weregild.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:14"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:19",
      "text": "Gunnar and Hogni are eager to lay down gold to atone for wrongs, and Grimhild asks who is willing to set forth on a journey with saddled steed, wain, hawk, and bow to shoot the arrow.",
      "category": "sequence",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:15"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:20",
      "text": "Valdarr the Dane-king, Jarisleif, Eymod, and Jarizskar enter in kingly fashion with the host of the Longbeards, wearing red cloaks, short-cut byrnie, strong hammered helms, girded with glaives, and having red-gleaming hair.",
      "category": "setting",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:16"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:21",
      "text": "Each of the visiting kings offers Gudrun desired gifts and pleasing speech, hoping to win back her trust, but she says she trusts none of them.",
      "category": "speech",
      "evidence_refs": ["ev:17"]
    },
    {
      "id": "obs:22",
      "text": "Grimhild brings Gudrun a beaker with a cold and bitter drink intended to quench the memory of wrongs.",
