      "id": "ev:2",
      "type": "summary",
      "locator": "lines 2995-3101",
      "quote_or_summary": "The story situates events in the forefathers’ time in a village called K’iákime (“Home of the Eagles”) under Thunder Mountain, now in ruins. In its earlier perfection, a beautiful maiden lived there, described as the daughter of the priest-chief.",
      "source_text_path": "texts/public-domain/zuni/project-gutenberg/zuni-folk-tales-cushing.md",
