      "rights_note": "Public domain; Project Gutenberg edition."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev:6",
      "type": "summary",
      "locator": "lines 2995-3101",
      "quote_or_summary": "The maiden wonders whose child it is, supposing that only a cruel mother would have deserted it in the spring, and expresses pity for the child who does not yet know it is alone. She decides to take it in her arms and care for it, speaks softly to it, carries it up the hill to her house, climbs the ladder, and brings it into the room where she sleeps.",
      "source_text_path": "texts/public-domain/zuni/project-gutenberg/zuni-folk-tales-cushing.md",
      "rights_note": "Public domain; Project Gutenberg edition."
